1. Windows structure, field and constant names
----------------------------------------------

The names and values of the Windows keyboard-layout structures, fields and constants used in this repository
(KBDTABLES, MODIFIERS, VK_TO_WCHAR_TABLE, DEADKEY, LIGATURE1, KLLF_ALTGR, WCH_DEAD, the VK_* virtual-key constants
and others) are taken from the `windows-sys` crate, version 0.61.2, module Win32::UI::Input::KeyboardAndMouse:

    https://crates.io/crates/windows-sys/0.61.2
    https://github.com/microsoft/windows-rs

`windows-sys` is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. Its copyright line, as required by those licences:

    Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.

Eight scan-code flag names (KBDEXT, KBDMULTIVK, KBDSPECIAL, KBDNUMPAD, KBDUNICODE, KBDINJECTEDVK, KBDMAPPEDVK,
KBDBREAK) are not part of that crate. Their names and values (0x0100 to 0x8000) are taken from FreeRDP's WinPR
header winpr/include/winpr/input.h, lines 30 to 37 at commit eb104c8689fec09bf94c6baac46fb585c3aa906f:

    https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/blob/eb104c8689fec09bf94c6baac46fb585c3aa906f/winpr/include/winpr/input.h#L30-L37

FreeRDP is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The copyright line of that file:

    Copyright 2012 Marc-Andre Moreau <marcandre.moreau@gmail.com>

The class and interface ids of the Shell link object (CLSID_ShellLink, IID_IShellLinkW, IID_IPersistFile) and the
positions of the methods the installer calls in the IUnknown, IShellLinkW and IPersistFile method tables
(installer/winhost/shortcut_windows.go) are taken from Microsoft's `windows` crate, version 0.61.3, modules
Win32::UI::Shell and Win32::System::Com, and its `windows-core` crate, version 0.61.2 (IUnknown):

    https://crates.io/crates/windows/0.61.3
    https://crates.io/crates/windows-core/0.61.2
    https://github.com/microsoft/windows-rs

Both are licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation, as above.

The values of the window, button, static, progress bar, font, message and registry constants and the field order
of WNDCLASSEXW, MSG and INITCOMMONCONTROLSEX used by the installers' wizard (installer/toolstub) are taken from the
same `windows` crate, version 0.61.3 (modules Win32::UI::WindowsAndMessaging, Win32::UI::Controls,
Win32::Graphics::Gdi, Win32::System::Com), with the function descriptions from Microsoft Learn.

Only the eight names and their values are used. No header of the Windows SDK or WDK is a source for any name.

2. Material from the YAKBD reference specification
--------------------------------------------------

The tool is written from the clean YAKBD reference specification, revision 10 (not public; tree of `spec/`
24fb0165bc1ef4c96c0b45c2859a933a9bd39e95), Copyright (c) 2026 The YAKBD contributors.
Its owner relicensed it, including its test inputs, to MIT-0 for use in the yakbd repositories on 2026-11-22.
Files taken from it:

- target/windows/vk/vk-names.tsv: from `spec/klc-format/tables/vk-names.tsv` (itself generated from the
  `windows-sys` VK_* constants, see section 1).
- testdata/reference-spec/: `.klc` test inputs written by the reference specification's authors for its MSKLC
  observations (folder `tests/`; the subfolder names give the source folder). Unchanged except line 2 of the
  `dll-format/` and `klc-format/` files, whose description text was made neutral.

- From the `.kbl.json` specification (yakbd/kbl-spec, MIT-0; prototype-history commit
  a264cf0 for the 0.1 schema, 0e76bf8 for the examples (unchanged since 858a7d9), Table A unchanged since 5fd540c;
  branch spec-0.2 at cf27333 for the 0.2 draft schema): format/kbljson/schema/0.1/kbl.schema.json, format/kbljson/schema/0.2/kbl.schema.json,
  target/windows/vk/windows-default-vk.tsv (Table A) and testdata/kbl-spec/examples/*.kbl.json, unchanged;
  testdata/kbl-spec/examples/cldr-pt-abnt2.kbl.json holds CLDR data under the Unicode License v3 (section 4).

3. Facts from public documentation
----------------------------------

The default virtual-key table, Table A (target/windows/vk/windows-default-vk.tsv), is the kbl specification's;
its rows rest on two public Microsoft Learn pages ("About Keyboard Input" and "Virtual-Key Codes", facts only)
and on the reference specification, as its header says.

The PE/COFF container is written from the public "PE Format" specification
(https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/pe-format) and the public resource-format pages cited in
the source files.

